  "core_idea": "**Myself** refers back to the speaker, either as the object of the speaker's own action or to show that it was the speaker, no one else.",
  "senses": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "reflexive",
      "definition": "used as the object of a verb or preposition when the action affects the speaker, the same person who is the subject",
      "explanation": "**Myself** is used when the subject and the object of the same clause refer to the same person: *I cut myself*. It is not just another way of saying **me**: use **me** when the object is a different person from the subject, *give it to me*, not *give it to myself*.",
